"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1669,"Narrated to us Yunus ibn 'Abd al-A'la, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who informed me 'Amr ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Bakr ibn Sawadah, that Abu al-Najib — the freed slave of 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'd — narrated to him that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (RA) narrated to him that it was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) garlic, onions, and leeks. It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, and the strongest of all that is garlic — do you forbid it?"" So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: *""Eat it. But whoever among you eats it, let him not approach this mosque until his odor has gone.""*

---

**CHAPTER:**"
